{
  "schema": "facttest-reference-routes/1",
  "law": "REFERENCE-AUTHORITY.md citation law and PASS1.md: living/editor documents govern current semantics; dated snapshots are historical unless explicitly pinned for reproducibility. Every file this table ingests is a REPRODUCIBILITY PIN of an authority at a recorded commit (git ls-remote head at ingest time), never the current authority itself. The register (REGISTER.json) carries the commit, blob id, sha256 and observation time of every copy.",
  "retrieval": {
    "problem": "the session egress policy denies every published authority host (CONNECT 403): doc.rust-lang.org, webassembly.github.io, gpuweb.github.io, w3c.github.io, html.spec.whatwg.org and the other *.spec.whatwg.org hosts, tc39.es, git-scm.com, www.w3.org, source.chromium.org, chromium.googlesource.com, raw.githack.com; D11-D13 could read sources pinned by commit only",
    "solution": "every denied published rendering that a publisher serves through GitHub Pages is the byte-exact content of that repository's gh-pages branch; that branch is reachable with exact commit identity through the session git proxy (git ls-remote / blobless partial fetch) and its files are fetchable immutably by commit from raw.githubusercontent.com, which the policy allows. Specification sources are taken from the publisher's default branch the same way. A published host without a Pages branch (WHATWG standards, doc.rust-lang.org, git-scm.com, www.w3.org/TR snapshots, Chromium code search) has NO_ROUTE for its rendering and is ingested as source only.",
    "allowed_route_hosts": [
      "raw.githubusercontent.com (HTTPS through the session proxy)",
      "github.com git smart-HTTP (through the session git proxy: ls-remote, partial fetch)"
    ],
    "not_claimed": "a file taken from a gh-pages branch was NOT observed at the published host; the register marks it PAGES_BRANCH and the published URL stays NOT_OBSERVED_AT_HOST until the policy admits the host"
  },
